==Strategy==
The showdown against Yulala can be a difficult challenge. Yulala moves faster than lightning, rapidly fires off devastating attacks that [[Warp|warp]] any survivors back by 1500 range, and despite his low range, his Omni Strike hits up to 400. Thankfully, the stage can also be rendered trivial with the right combination of units and a few items.

By constantly spamming [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]]s with perfect timing, Yulala can be held in place, but extreme caution must be taken, and countermeasures must be in place to ensure the peons don't get in your way. [[:Category:Cats with Warp Immunity|Immune to Warp Cats]] can be considered, but players should use Cats that can take multiple hits, such as [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] and [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Dogumaru]].

Keeping Yulala [[slow]]ed is another helpful way at controlling his pace across the battlefield. [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]] is very good for this, but players can also use [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]], both of which outrange Yulala and can keep him slowed. The Slow effect does not last without massive stacks of these Cats, however, so other means of pinning Yulala is necessary.

As such, [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Lone Cat and Kitten]], [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]], and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] are all helpful here thanks to their [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] abilities. Glass and Lone Cat can further stall Yulala, and push him back further when [[True Form]]ed. When True Formed, Macho Crystal Cat slows Yulala for 10 seconds, and his cooldown time is about 21 seconds. This means that the stalling required to kill Yulala is effectively halved. On his cooldown, Tourist Cat can aid your units by pushing Yulala while Glass is on cooldown. These greatly reduce the difficulty of Yulala, making his stage much more manageable.

If timed correctly, certain units such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] and [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] can deal insane amounts of damage to Yulala in seconds. Slime Cat in particular is extremely effective in getting rid of mass hordes of oncoming peons with its devastating [[Wave Attack]] nearly one-shotting the Gabriels at high levels. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] is a great option, at level 40 it can crash into Yulala up to 3 times as it gets warped back while also getting extra money if it kills any peons.

On subsequent clears, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] at Lv.40 (using a small Attack UP [[Cat Combo]]) and with maxed Explosion [[Talents|Talent]], can be used in tandem with [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] to speedrun the stage.

